# .env.example — environment variables for the NFL model project.
#
# The production pipeline requires NO secrets. All data sources are
# keyless public endpoints (nflverse data, ESPN public API, Bovada public
# coupon API). No API keys, passwords, tokens, or private credentials
# are used anywhere in the production code.
#
# This file exists only as a documented placeholder so that:
#   1. contributors can see at a glance that nothing secret is needed, and
#   2. if a future (explicitly approved) integration ever needs a secret,
#      there is a clear place to name it — while .gitignore keeps any
#      real .env file out of the repository.
#
# Example (currently unused):
# OPTIONAL_SERVICE_API_KEY=
